From 480285832bfc50e6df23de7caecee5dcf2273f23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omesh <roland@nordhain.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 19:56:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/41] feat: parallel fast_refresh DIRECT-BULK hash lookup +
 PERF logging
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- get_hashes: new path for empty block_ids + start_height > 0 using
  BlockHashInRange (rayon-parallel LMDB read), up to 100k hashes per
  request (3.2MB, 10x fewer round-trips than 10k batches)
- get_blocks: handle empty block_ids with start_height > 0 (previously
  errored) — required for pull_blocks_extra parallel prefetch
- route/bin.rs: request counter (active + total), per-request BEGIN/END
  timing, gzip compression timing microseconds and ratio
- detailed [PERF GB]/[PERF RPC] logs to pinpoint bottlenecks between
  server handler and wallet client

Used in conjunction with the wallet fast_refresh parallelisation:
servers returns 100k hashes per request, wallet spawns up to 8 parallel
pull_hashes_extra threads → fast_refresh drops from ~6min to ~40s.
